    "title": "Next.js Developer with Headless CMS Experience",
    "ciphertext": "~022079895315289419908",
    "description": "Next.js Developer with Headless CMS Experience (Sanity Preferred)\n\nWe are looking for an experienced freelance/fractional developer to support an existing Next.js website with a headless CMS backend.\n\nThe ideal candidate has strong production experience with Next.js and React, along with hands-on experience using Sanity CMS (preferred), Contentful, or another modern headless CMS.\n\nThis is an ongoing part-time engagement focused on maintaining and improving an existing website, developing new pages and reusable components, supporting post-launch improvements, and collaborating with our team during US Eastern Time business hours.\n\nResponsibilities\n- Build and maintain pages, components, templates, and site features using Next.js\n- Work with a headless CMS such as Sanity or Contentful\n- Improve reusable page sections, content models, and editor workflows\n- Implement rich text / Portable Text rendering with custom components\n- Support post-launch QA, bug fixes, and content updates\n- Help with SEO improvements, metadata, redirects, and validation\n- Support caching, preview, publishing, and deployment workflows\n- Create and update campaign pages when needed\n\nRequired Skills\n- Strong React and Next.js experience (App Router preferred)\n- Production experience with Sanity CMS (preferred), Contentful, or another headless CMS\n- TypeScript\n- Experience building reusable components and page templates\n- Familiarity with structured content models, CMS APIs, queries, references, and rich text rendering\n- Understanding of SEO best practices for production websites\n- Strong written communication and ability to work independently\n\nNice to Have\n- Sanity schemas, GROQ, Portable Text, and Studio customization\n- Vercel deployments\n- Webhook-based revalidation / ISR\n- Experience supporting post-launch website maintenance\n- Experience building marketing or campaign landing pages\n\nPlease include with your proposal\n- A live production Next.js + Headless CMS project you personally worked on.\n- Which CMS you used and what you personally implemented.\n- A GitHub repository, code sample, or screenshots (if available).\n- A brief summary of your experience with Sanity CMS, Contentful, or similar platforms.\n- Your hourly rate, weekly availability, and ET overlap.\n\nPlease do not apply if your experience with headless CMS is limited to tutorials, starter templates, or demo projects.",
